README = _release_expand(f"""This demon makes the archive's source claims trialable against primary numbers and holds knows what the figure actually measures. It delivers {len(obs)} verified measurement facets from {len(groups)} studies and a review draft {m['unique_existing_edges_with_scoped_facits']} existing R4 edges. Numerical calibration of the target models remains.\n\nRun from this directory:\n\n```bash\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nExecution uses frozen report extracts and primary sources already in `@DENTAL_WORK_ROOT@/XFACIT-harvest/sources`. No network access is needed for the demon. Python, NumPy , lxml and BeautifulSoup are used for the controls; the figure uses the system's Matplotlib through `python3 -s` . No package installation or global environmental change is made. All calculations use a thread.\n\nAfter final binding, the `results.json` rerun will preserve and check that the scientific values and artifact hashs are identical. New running cost is written in `REPLAY_RESULTS.json` and check in `REPLAY_VERIFICATION.json` ; the review binding hash does not change.\n\nThe idea is that an observation needs source , exact locator, quantity , device, statistics, population, protocol, site and time. A primary table first passes a numeric check and then a control of which the query observation may respond. For example, a group average may respond to a query if the group; a local column field requires local measurement .\n\n| Results | Outcome | Resolution |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Frozen external_referent entries, including the archive | {h['counts']['referents']} | PHENOMENOLOGICAL : archive counting |\n| Independently reviewed report candidates | {h['selected_reports']} | PHENOMENOLOGICAL: reports |\n| Candidates with verified primary figures | {h['reports_with_primary_facets']} | PHENOMENOLOGICAL: reports |\n| Candidates without numerical reference | {h['reports_without_primary_facets']} ({100 * h['rejection_fraction']:.2f} %) | PHENOMENOLOGICAL: reports |\n| Different primary/numerical measurement facets | {len(groups)} / {len(obs)} | Study level; facets has its own resolution |\n| Edges with draft source facit / directly affected K chains | {m['unique_existing_edges_with_scoped_facits']} / {m['direct_K_consumer_count']} | PHENOMENOLOGICAL : network count |\n| Calibrated physical Edges / passed Target Range | 0 / 0 | PHENOMENOLOGICAL: gate outcomes |\n| Rejected injected value and metadata errors | {r['source_control']['wrong_value_and_metadata_rejected']} / {r['source_control']['injected_faults']} | PHENOMENOLOGICAL : controls |\n| Satisfaction test: identity error / regional difference | 0 / 87,68 µm | Exact summary; POPULATION with PER_SURFACE_REGION - support |\n\nExamples of decided queries :\n\n| Question | Primary factor and consequence |\n|---|---|\n| Is the archived powder temperature 527,45 ° C ? | Table 2 shows separately n=5 and 27,45 °C. The value 527,45 is a merge. POPULATION with PER_POINT - support . [Primary source](https://doi.org/10.3390/dj11080197). |\n| Is the total margin column sufficient for a given region? | Table 2 : LD vestibular 111,64 and palatal 23,96 µm . A constructed change of region labels retains the full range and mean 62,28 µm exactly, but changes the vestibular issue with 87,68 µm . POPULATION with PER_SURFACE_REGION - support . [Primary source](https://doi.org/10.3390/ma16062413). |\n| Did the crown study measure the effect of an even thickness from 1 to 3 mm ? | Methods: the 3 mm group has 1 mm occlusal , 3 mm proximal and prefabricated abutment; the others have individually manufactured abutment. The table cannot isolate the proposed thickness effect. [Primary source](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-023-03100-0). |\n| Can the new drilling table calibrate paired temperature increases? | Table 2 : Group A provides 23,41 − 20,98 − 2,00 = 0,43 K and B provides 24,00 − 20,94 − 3,44 = − 0,38 K . Both are located outside the ± 0,015 K of pressure rounding. The same paired population is assumed; the source is kept in quarantine. [Primary source](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-025-06593-z). |\n| Can seven preloads be treated as measurements at the same moment? | The primary abstract indicates the manufacturer-recommended components of different systems. Systemic agents 181,6 – 643,4 N must not be compared as a common 35 Ncm protocol. POPULATION with PER_TOOTH - support . [Primary source](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11432656/). |\n\n![ Reference , Summary Collision and Remaining Calibration Gap](FACIT_HARVEST.png)\n\nWhat does not holds is automatic transmission from literature statistics to the field of its own design, fracture quintile, thermal history or healing. All proposed bindings have `PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW` and refrain from physical numerical assignment when target protocol or finite reasonableness interval is missing. Manual rules or clinical decisions have not been validated. The frozen laboratory example of a 100 µm - boundary is an illustrative query, no clinical boundary.\n\nThe comparison applies to `information_link`: previous practice here was the report's flag and free text, while R4 had 15 source observations from three studies. Now there are primary cells, units and protocols that can reject specific claims. The equally informed control reads the same primary values directly and matches them; no algorithm advantage is claimed. `FROZEN_PREDICTIONS.json` freezes archive claims prior to source review, not a blind physical prediction. R2 and R3B report that their already exposed numbers are used in retrospective controls.\n\nReference is available in `VERIFIED_OBSERVATIONS.jsonl` , each report score in `VERIFICATIONS.jsonl` , all archive extract in `EXTRACTED_FACIT_CANDIDATES.jsonl` and the target interval status in `RANGE_CHECKS.json` . De {h['counts']['referents'] - h['selected_reports']} the other reference entries are extracted but lack individual primary examination. More quoted sources in an reviewed report is not automatically verified.\n\nThe data sources are published experimental tables and abstracts, with rights data per study in `SOURCE_LICENSES.json` . CC BY / CC BY - NC / CC BY - NC - ND is only given when the source itself indicates it; missing license is held UNKNOWN and the source copy is used for local review . No patient data sets, mesh archives or personal data are used. Repeated reports and multiple cells from the same study do not provide new independent experiments. `COST_LEDGER.json` reports logged source calls , control cost and costs that could not be counted accurately.\n""")
