RESULTS = f"Forty of 52 audited report candidates provide verified primary figures. The 269 measurement facets from 30 studies can be used as source bound references in a draft for 24 existing edges and 22 K chains. The Reference determines, among other things, fault parsing of temperature, wrong tooth arch, mixed tensile strength and a faulty thickness experiment.\n\nThe main claim is `information_link`; source statement, derivation, published parameterfit and own counter-example design have separate roles. Precise primary locator, hash, unit, population, protocol and resolution follow each observation. All result and links await independent review.\n\nR1 harvested all 873 valid reference entries from 3716 readable reports. 239 bar `refutes_us=true` ; 1720 dual paths were deduplicated. Four JSON files could not be read and a external_referent structure was incorrect. The harvest uses targeted paths and does not follow a recursive archive hike. The archive task that the briefen specifies is thus an older estimate, not the frozen calculator here. `CORPUS_MANIFEST.json` contains loss and reporthashar.\n\nThe first 40 priority candidates were reviewed all ; 29 gave primary figures. R3 broadened to missing preload, fatigue and interface protocols with eleven new frozen candidates . One of these failed on an exact mating identity; R3B then examined a separate cooling source. The original negative gates remain and were not replaced.\n\nSlutligt attrition: {h['reports_without_primary_facets']}/{h['selected_reports']}={100 * h['rejection_fraction']:.4f} % of the report candidates. Reasons under the operative file: {json.dumps(dict(withheld), ensure_ascii=False)}. This is not a random selection and no estimate of the general error rate of the archive.\n\nThe adequacy test uses four published regional LD mean values. A and a constructed B have identical full range, n, mean, variance, min and max with float64 - identity error 0 . The vestibular question distinguishes 87,68 µm. The minimum extension for the query is region label plus associated average; arbitrary regional queries requires the entire region→median map. An individual column field requires point coordinates and measurements . B is a counter-example, not another measured specimen. No affinity physical sensitivity or physical enclosure claimed.\n\nThe exact mating control in `SOURCE_BALANCE.json` provides residual intervals [0,415 ; 0,445 ] K and [ − 0,395 ; − 0,365 ] K for two groups; zero is not included. The range refers only to pressure rounding for the same paired agents. Measurement bias and possible different selections for the three columns are UNKNOWN . The source is therefore kept outside calibration , without guessing a corrected figure.\n\nControl outcomes : all 269 correct source values were accepted and all 1614 injected errors into value , device, locator, context, sourcehash or spread label were rejected. Ten typed queries , including a permitted regional query and nine unauthorized transfers, gave pre-registered behavior. The mating control accepted a consistent triple and rejected one injected Δ T=999. Seven PDF lines are based on visual primary review; the re-entry checks the transcript, not a new visual reading. Direct extraction with the same information matches the source values.\n\nThe 606 observation-edge proposal of the draft concerns: {', '.join(m['existing_edge_ids'])}. All retains R4's SIMULTANEOUS/HANDOVER contract. A thermal end does not replace a history or a healing stroke. The facets are 215 POPULATION statistics, 40 PER_POINT interface readings and 14 PER_TOOTH test loads/cycle ends; support region and method follow each entry.\n\n**Physically target output:** zero calibrated edges and zero new numerical target range. The work adds auditable source references and queries that can now be convicted. Source and goal do not yet share a fully verified protocol. `plausible_range` distinguishes mathematical domain, printed source cell housing and a true target range. They must not be mixed.\n\nThe draft decision concerns: regional margin adjustment/cementation K43 / K44 / K48 ; material, support and tensile selection K32 / K36 / K49 ; pre-assembly and testing K20 / K33 / K38 ; local interface measurement K19 / K26 / K27 / K31 ; tooth load and arc identity K15 / K16 / K21 ; PDL : s loading conditions K13 / K17 ; as well as cooling, drilling heat and temperature history K23 / K24 / K28 . It's source and measurement protocol decisions. No manufacturing design or clinical design has been approved by these links.\n\nCost of the final control run: {r['cost']['run_wall_s']:.2f} s wall time, {r['cost']['run_CPU_s']:.2f} s CPU and {r['cost']['max_rss_kib'] / 1024:.1f} MiB maximum reported RSS for the control process; 1 thread, no GPU or fit. Source cache {r['cost']['source_storage_bytes'] / 1000000.0:.2f} MB. Source search and annotation are included in the time from first PREREG ({r['cost']['preparation_discovery_validation_wall_s_from_prereg'] / 60:.1f} min at this execution ; preparation before the time stamp and token cost is UNKNOWN . Demon does not download sources and does not ask human questions. `COST_LEDGER.json` complements with logged source calls and documented cost gaps. Recurrent failures and exact run commands are found in `COMMANDS.md`.\n"
(P / 'RESULTS.md').write_text(RESULTS)
